Package: warp-im
Version: {{VERSION}}
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: {{ARCH}}
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libgcc-s1 (>= 3.0), libstdc++6 (>= 5)
Maintainer: Rubens Rainelli <rubens@rainelli.it>
Homepage: https://github.com/RubensRainelli/warp-im
Description: Universal Native Multi-Protocol Messenger (PEFL v1.0)
 Warp IM is an ultra-low-memory (< 50 MB RAM), GPU-accelerated native
 messenger written in Rust and Slint unifying 8 messaging protocols:
 Telegram (MTProto), Matrix (Megolm), XMPP (OMEMO), Nostr (NIP-17),
 SimpleX Chat (SMP), IRCv3 (Soju/Ergo), Stoat, and Mattermost.
 .
 Features hot-swappable SuperThemes (Telegram, WhatsApp, Discord, IRC Dense),
 6 color palettes (Light, Dark, OLED Pure Black, Night Telegram, Discord Dark,
 Catppuccin Mocha), multi-account per protocol, and 4 chat list isolation modes.
 .
